      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear you—this isn't a pause, it's a hollow that feels permanent, and that's a terrifying place to stand. But a dry well isn't proof the water is gone; it's proof the ground has shifted, and sometimes you have to dig a new channel instead of waiting for the old one to refill. The role you're performing might be the very thing suffocating the color—what would happen if you let that role crack, even just a little? You don't have to find the color today; you just have to stop pretending the void isn't real.",
